<title>UK: BOE invites fixed rate ops, shortage 950 mln stg.</title>
<headline>BOE invites fixed rate ops, shortage 950 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England invited a round of fixed rate operations from UK money market operators to help alleviate a forecast 950 million stg liquidity shortage in the market.</p>
<p>The operations will comprise repos to March 25 and 26 and outright offers of bills maturing on or before March 26.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5109</p>
